    "s1": {
      "fill": "blue",
      "text": "Hierarchy for implementation:\nJarvis (global assistant, 1 per app)\n  → Workspace (project folder + git repo)\n    → Orchestrator (1 per workspace, plans & delegates)\n      → Agents (role, model, skills, integrations)\n        → Tasks → Runs → Changes (branch) → QA → Merge\n\nShell: full-window isometric scene (LobbyScene or OfficeScene) + Hud (floating top bar + bottom dock) + one Drawer panel on the right. Panels never replace the world; they slide over it.",
      "w": 520,
      "x": -640,
      "y": 0
    },
    "s2": {
      "fill": "orange",
      "text": "Approval rule: anything that sends, merges, deletes, bills or touches folders lands in Inbox (03) unless the integration/agent policy says 'auto'.",
      "w": 520,
      "x": -640,
      "y": 1420
    },
    "s3": {
      "fill": "teal",
      "text": "C1/C2 are drawn on the canvas with divs, but in the app they are Three.js worlds: OrthographicCamera at yaw 45° / pitch −35.264°, 1 tile = 1 world unit. Exact positions of every desk, zone, prop and label are in handoff/office-layout.json and handoff/lobby-layout.json. Labels are Vue components inside CSS2DObjects so they stay clickable and accessible. See board 15.",
      "w": 520,
      "x": -640,
      "y": 7750
    },
